From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:05:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dt-bindings: clock: qcom,sm8550-dispcc: Add the MX power
 domain on Kaanapali

The display clock controller of Kaanapali (SM8850) has its PLLs on the MX
rail, as the vendor tree describes it (dispcc: vdd_mm and vdd_mx). The PLL
that feeds the MDP core clock runs at three times the MDP rate, up to
1.95 GHz for 650 MHz, and needs MX at its corner while it runs.

Allow a second power domain and performance point (MX) for
qcom,kaanapali-dispcc, as the multi-domain camera and video clock
controllers do (MMCX + MXC). The other compatibles keep exactly one.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/clock/qcom,sm8550-dispcc.yaml    | 26 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm8550-dispcc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm8550-dispcc.yaml
index 61f58fbd5bd2..7b0def2fc970 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm8550-dispcc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm8550-dispcc.yaml
@@ -54,14 +54,16 @@ properties:
       - description: VCO DIV clock from DP PHY3
 
   power-domains:
-    description:
-      A phandle and PM domain specifier for the MMCX power domain.
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: MMCX power domain
+      - description: MX power domain
 
   required-opps:
-    description:
-      A phandle to an OPP node describing required MMCX performance point.
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: MMCX performance point
+      - description: MX performance point
 
 required:
   - compatible
@@ -70,6 +72,18 @@ required:
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: qcom,gcc.yaml#
+  - if:
+      not:
+        properties:
+          compatible:
+            contains:
+              const: qcom,kaanapali-dispcc
+    then:
+      properties:
+        power-domains:
+          maxItems: 1
+        required-opps:
+          maxItems: 1
 
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
